{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "With Heroku’s latest pricing restructure announcement, I decided it was time to re-evaluate my side-project hosting strategies.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e616193b7ec6970c95df73b0ea85b2931bb61b0af99669dd8599a2d00744714d.mp3"}, {"text": "Historically, Heroku has been my go to as a hosting provider for my various rails application endeavors, because it is so easy to setup and, most importantly, free.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8b1e7110de762f55b99093b452de46d3d42bfd688e499ba92cecbde341f40ed9.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.66], [1, 1.16, 1.42], [2, 1.42, 1.62], [3, 1.62, 1.74], [4, 1.74, 1.9], [5, 1.9, 2.08], [7, 2.28, 2.5], [8, 2.5, 2.58], [9, 2.58, 2.9], [10, 2.9, 3.3], [11, 3.3, 3.58], [12, 3.58, 3.7], [13, 3.7, 4.08], [14, 4.08, 4.36], [15, 4.36, 4.94], [16, 4.94, 5.3], [17, 5.3, 6.26], [18, 6.26, 6.38], [19, 6.38, 6.52], [20, 6.52, 6.7], [21, 6.7, 7.04], [22, 7.04, 7.22], [24, 7.6, 7.96], [25, 7.96, 8.26], [26, 8.26, 8.78], [27, 9.2, 9.32]]}, {"text": "Previously my strategy for free hosting on Heroku without any server sleeping was to configure new relic to measure server uptime.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f72f668e407e3651c4a39bb55bfbfead1173b1e345ead074a9f17251c624df85.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.58], [3, 1.16, 1.5], [4, 1.5, 1.74], [5, 1.74, 2.1], [6, 2.1, 2.3], [7, 2.3, 2.66], [8, 2.66, 2.94], [9, 2.94, 3.2], [10, 3.2, 3.48], [12, 3.96, 4.54], [13, 4.54, 4.7], [14, 4.7, 5.1], [15, 5.1, 5.4], [16, 5.4, 5.8], [17, 5.8, 5.96], [18, 5.96, 6.2], [19, 6.2, 6.62], [20, 6.62, 7.06]]}, {"text": "This was a great trick to keep your Heroku server from sleeping and it let you keep an eye out for server down time.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/37bdee0014f56a3b2646e64f77c25eba95c6ba806efbf8970c1cb5abbf1c6716.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [2, 0.3, 0.42], [3, 0.42, 0.58], [4, 0.58, 0.86], [5, 0.86, 1.06], [6, 1.06, 1.28], [7, 1.28, 1.46], [8, 1.46, 1.84], [9, 1.84, 2.16], [10, 2.16, 2.44], [11, 2.44, 2.8], [13, 3.02, 3.1], [14, 3.1, 3.22], [15, 3.22, 3.4], [16, 3.4, 3.56], [17, 3.56, 3.76], [18, 3.76, 3.92], [19, 3.92, 4.1], [20, 4.1, 4.26], [21, 4.26, 4.54]]}, {"text": "I shall be sad to see that go :(.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d33aa20739f5331309ba07ffd496872d3addb1ca3de9f3bfff6870dc143c7852.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.52], [3, 0.52, 0.8], [4, 0.8, 0.96], [5, 0.96, 1.12], [6, 1.12, 1.3], [7, 1.3, 1.52]]}, {"text": "My new recipe for creating new side project deployments is as follows:", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d10f4a1009334efb4262f1c6c72395ffb33c992244976299410228f66976bd8a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.74], [3, 0.74, 0.96], [4, 0.96, 1.26], [7, 1.68, 2.04], [8, 2.04, 2.62], [9, 2.62, 2.8], [10, 2.8, 2.94], [11, 2.94, 3.3]]}, {"text": "Buying a domain for free", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/647d91a6ee24275b9db832d12eef8c1f2137cb12e6ef7915b68de28db0e8216d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.36, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.76], [3, 0.76, 1.08], [4, 1.08, 1.38]]}, {"text": "With the new influx of TLD extensions, many registrars are heavily discounting these new extensions in order to encourage main stream adoption.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8842ace88c1c1904ae9d64dd9f4d5684ad259415d38685d943349b8c23735b93.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.54], [3, 0.54, 1.04], [4, 1.04, 1.22], [5, 1.22, 1.64], [6, 1.64, 2.18], [7, 2.78, 2.96], [8, 2.96, 3.54], [9, 3.54, 3.7], [10, 3.7, 4.04], [11, 4.04, 4.72], [12, 4.72, 4.9], [13, 4.9, 5.04], [14, 5.04, 5.52], [15, 5.52, 5.86], [16, 5.86, 6.12], [17, 6.12, 6.34], [18, 6.34, 6.76], [21, 7.14, 7.72]]}, {"text": "You can snag a new domain name for dirt cheap, and often free, using one of these new domain extensions.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/991a37102f89b97feb95f2cfeeb1f1882e8e67f53c1cd1ba0d20308828540b15.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.82], [3, 0.82, 1.02], [4, 1.02, 1.2], [5, 1.2, 1.46], [6, 1.46, 1.74], [7, 1.74, 2.02], [8, 2.02, 2.22], [9, 2.22, 2.58], [10, 2.58, 3.08], [11, 3.08, 3.4], [12, 3.4, 3.76], [13, 3.76, 4.18], [14, 4.18, 4.4], [15, 4.4, 4.5], [16, 4.5, 4.7], [17, 4.7, 4.84], [18, 4.84, 5.16], [19, 5.16, 5.68]]}, {"text": "If you are still a student or still have a .edu email address (thanks, Georgia Tech!), you can register a .me domain for free and/or a heavily discounted .com or .io domain using Github.com’s education pack.", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c445c52591c7e3bb16677a6cf4d7be2ba56277c046e908c0bb480c925b0d1da9.mp3"}, {"text": "Checkout register.science, register.party, and get on the Alpnames mailing list to be notified of when free domain names are available for registration.", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e41dbe62d3e01e11b6dad15842f919fbf86d60f5f409e30c5c35b7501b9b546c.mp3"}, {"text": "Hosting", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/6d8b5b9bc5b6722199c366cf77be54cb572f1116ef5935473f7eccba0117c6d9.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.68]]}, {"text": "Heroku (free-ish)", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/368c15c9072cd86385d6872d8d34d94ea6a8fdd03fd5c08a5ac1b873959c0a56.mp3"}, {"text": "You can stick with Heroku dyno’s but like I said before, they are no longer allow websites to be active 24 per day.", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/de2e50d4d9b0669c75d20dc4168ff90c36e1566ccde386af2230fa2f0915d53e.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.26], [2, 0.26, 0.46], [3, 0.46, 0.68], [4, 0.68, 1.0], [6, 1.64, 1.7], [7, 1.7, 1.96], [8, 1.96, 2.12], [9, 2.12, 2.28], [10, 2.28, 2.66], [11, 3.06, 3.14], [12, 3.14, 3.22], [13, 3.22, 3.36], [14, 3.36, 3.68], [15, 3.68, 3.92], [16, 3.92, 4.34], [17, 4.34, 4.64], [18, 4.64, 4.74], [19, 4.74, 5.06], [20, 5.06, 5.5], [21, 5.5, 5.84], [22, 5.84, 6.04]]}, {"text": "Heroku will still be my go to for scheduled rake tasks, or anything that doesn’t need to be awake all day since it is so easy to deploy to.", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5200e3b92b456ee51155a3d6504ead7012240154a1c805a29885557e7c0aa0e4.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.4], [1, 0.4, 0.6], [2, 0.6, 0.9], [3, 0.9, 1.1], [4, 1.1, 1.28], [5, 1.28, 1.48], [6, 1.48, 1.66], [7, 1.66, 1.92], [8, 1.92, 2.32], [9, 2.32, 2.6], [10, 2.6, 3.04], [11, 3.44, 3.64], [12, 3.64, 4.0], [13, 4.0, 4.2], [14, 4.2, 4.52], [15, 4.52, 4.64], [16, 4.64, 4.8], [17, 4.8, 4.92], [18, 4.92, 5.16], [19, 5.16, 5.4], [20, 5.4, 5.64], [21, 5.64, 5.9], [22, 5.9, 6.08], [23, 6.08, 6.2], [24, 6.2, 6.4], [25, 6.4, 6.74], [26, 6.74, 6.94], [27, 6.94, 7.2], [28, 7.2, 7.52]]}, {"text": "Heroku also has great free database hosting for side projects.", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f01589d8bea46782893380ee32921229c89929a4c9a40f79eec4ca8521341dee.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.58, 0.94], [2, 0.94, 1.18], [3, 1.18, 1.38], [4, 1.38, 1.64], [5, 1.64, 1.94], [6, 1.94, 2.44], [7, 2.44, 2.68], [8, 2.68, 2.88], [9, 2.88, 3.26]]}, {"text": "As long as your db doesn’t exceed 10,000 rows, Heroku will host it for free and give you a nice interface to run queries on.", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1b878f907b45ae82d91fc1740d9a7e55f90b017ce23bb76a904d19903f15795b.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [1, 0.3, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.7], [4, 0.7, 0.9], [5, 0.9, 1.3], [6, 1.3, 1.56], [8, 2.26, 2.52], [9, 2.78, 3.06], [10, 3.06, 3.26], [11, 3.26, 3.52], [12, 3.52, 3.64], [13, 3.64, 3.78], [14, 3.78, 4.08], [15, 4.08, 4.3], [16, 4.3, 4.48], [17, 4.48, 4.64], [18, 4.64, 4.74], [19, 4.74, 4.94], [20, 4.94, 5.42], [21, 5.42, 5.7], [22, 5.7, 5.86], [23, 5.86, 6.18], [24, 6.18, 6.48]]}, {"text": "Apigee (free)", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/90150cc65fd9f7aeaf39c8a0ed00f1dc934829b40c1c88eb999290f97ea4bda7.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.58], [1, 0.98, 1.32]]}, {"text": "Apigee Edge promises a lot of really nice features for their developer accounts: a buttload of storage space, unlimited bandwidth, and api analytics.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/25c2246d2b64dd4c628bb9b85724af0ae64c8011201706fdc5357baf6fc06f77.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.48], [1, 0.48, 0.76], [2, 0.76, 1.14], [3, 1.14, 1.46], [4, 1.46, 1.68], [5, 1.68, 1.86], [6, 1.86, 2.08], [7, 2.08, 2.28], [8, 2.28, 2.64], [9, 2.64, 2.98], [10, 2.98, 3.14], [11, 3.14, 3.54], [12, 3.54, 4.04], [13, 4.54, 4.6], [14, 4.6, 5.0], [15, 5.0, 5.2], [16, 5.2, 5.48], [17, 5.48, 5.92], [18, 6.2, 6.48], [19, 6.48, 6.94], [21, 7.42, 7.78], [22, 7.78, 8.24]]}, {"text": "The big gotcha’s though are they only host nodejs applications and their documentation is terrible.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c06fff71ac3a478d2737b1e2e33890452392a2bb4521d6df839e0e14e08c1fa1.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.42], [2, 0.42, 0.8], [3, 0.8, 1.1], [4, 1.1, 1.42], [5, 1.42, 1.58], [6, 1.58, 1.8], [7, 1.8, 2.1], [9, 2.56, 3.08], [10, 3.08, 3.44], [11, 3.44, 3.54], [12, 3.54, 4.04], [13, 4.04, 4.5], [14, 4.5, 4.9]]}, {"text": "Once if you can figure out how to get your website running, it is pretty simple to maintain, but getting it up there may take hours.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b5ff23412b7570a05a4513d12312d8a2e3f3619d3c2008755ab241ae8b779eca.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [2, 0.24, 0.46], [3, 0.46, 0.6], [4, 0.6, 0.88], [5, 0.88, 1.08], [6, 1.08, 1.26], [7, 1.26, 1.34], [8, 1.34, 1.48], [9, 1.48, 1.62], [10, 1.62, 1.92], [11, 1.92, 2.32], [12, 2.62, 2.64], [13, 2.64, 2.76], [14, 2.76, 3.0], [15, 3.0, 3.4], [16, 3.4, 3.62], [17, 3.62, 4.06], [18, 4.62, 4.74], [19, 4.74, 4.92], [20, 4.92, 5.12], [21, 5.12, 5.18], [22, 5.18, 5.36], [23, 5.36, 5.52], [24, 5.52, 5.74], [25, 5.74, 6.16]]}, {"text": "I used them for the Sears Hackathon and the struggle was real.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/6299aee5dd8b8fce8de1e9971c472279ffebb6968123b2dddd3e232ea273032e.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.64], [3, 0.64, 0.86], [5, 1.04, 1.42], [6, 1.42, 1.92], [7, 1.92, 2.22], [8, 2.22, 2.32], [9, 2.32, 2.62], [10, 2.62, 2.86], [11, 2.86, 3.1]]}, {"text": "You can also do some pretty sweet stuff with combining api’s into new apis.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a792497c59e1ca3e91412fe16c2e8415eef47eb47bd778f23db3c875c2fced55.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.28], [2, 0.28, 0.5], [3, 0.5, 0.64], [4, 0.64, 0.76], [5, 0.76, 0.98], [6, 0.98, 1.18], [7, 1.18, 1.5], [8, 1.5, 1.72], [9, 1.72, 2.12], [11, 2.56, 2.86], [12, 2.86, 3.06], [13, 3.06, 3.36]]}, {"text": "They also have a service that competes with Parse for managing mobile app data, but again, the documentation is terrible.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a7fb21aa5ff2b8dc3f970ea07ede6794c8950019d387eb61dcf2e6100e9b00a8.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.74], [3, 0.74, 0.86], [4, 0.86, 1.14], [5, 1.14, 1.42], [6, 1.42, 1.84], [7, 1.84, 2.0], [9, 2.24, 2.44], [10, 2.44, 2.76], [11, 2.76, 3.1], [12, 3.1, 3.44], [13, 3.44, 3.72], [14, 4.26, 4.46], [15, 4.46, 4.72], [16, 5.04, 5.1], [17, 5.1, 5.62], [18, 5.62, 6.16], [19, 6.16, 6.58]]}, {"text": "Good luck.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/6205504968977fa946eb3f583ec9ec4ad2130b3a869ff79cd2d3bc065603bcd3.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.4]]}, {"text": "Github pages (free)", "block": 14, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/dc82cb3a36e3f85aec959d9b735259280730165e50959ae781f9e8bd8e8f5302.mp3"}, {"text": "I host this blog on Github pages and build things with Octopress.", "block": 15, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/4f8eb8e18faf7eb71fa8015cb708a0318d194af7b8729efd786f71408a1d5bfa.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.52], [3, 0.52, 0.84], [4, 0.84, 1.08], [5, 1.08, 1.32], [6, 1.32, 1.78], [7, 1.78, 2.04], [9, 2.22, 2.46], [10, 2.46, 2.72], [11, 2.72, 3.2]]}, {"text": "Deployments and settings things up are a breeze, but github only hosts static content.", "block": 15, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/bde845fc3e5e260317ba694f6b9898b5c04009398b057673027795850099183c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.58], [1, 0.58, 0.78], [2, 0.78, 1.06], [3, 1.06, 1.3], [4, 1.3, 1.54], [5, 1.54, 1.78], [6, 1.78, 1.88], [7, 1.88, 2.14], [8, 2.6, 2.76], [9, 2.76, 3.04], [10, 3.04, 3.44], [11, 3.44, 3.66], [12, 3.66, 4.04], [13, 4.04, 4.44]]}, {"text": "A small part of me is considering moving AtlantaStartupJobs.com to github, because the content there only changes once per day.", "block": 16, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/63dd0273ab70751426ead3a9ebded43a4181878782757c2bf7c70a2eadc09079.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.62], [3, 0.62, 0.76], [4, 0.76, 0.86], [5, 0.86, 1.0], [6, 1.0, 1.4], [7, 1.4, 1.82], [9, 3.5, 3.86], [10, 3.86, 4.12], [11, 4.5, 4.82], [12, 4.82, 4.98], [13, 4.98, 5.28], [14, 5.28, 5.52], [15, 5.52, 5.82], [16, 5.82, 6.2], [17, 6.2, 6.52], [18, 6.52, 6.76], [19, 6.76, 6.98]]}, {"text": "I would just need to write ruby tasks to grab the latest Atlanta start up jobs, generate the html for them, and then push up to Github.", "block": 16, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/cc65b3bcf86fcf9394150df4f475ebb62bc716e6a878c9b2add0a06f7e36d79c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.44], [3, 0.44, 0.68], [4, 0.68, 0.86], [5, 0.86, 1.04], [6, 1.04, 1.28], [7, 1.28, 1.86], [8, 1.86, 2.06], [9, 2.06, 2.24], [10, 2.24, 2.46], [11, 2.46, 2.72], [12, 2.72, 3.06], [15, 3.46, 3.98], [16, 4.26, 4.62], [17, 4.62, 4.8], [18, 4.8, 5.2], [19, 5.2, 5.54], [20, 5.54, 5.76], [21, 5.98, 6.08], [22, 6.08, 6.22], [23, 6.22, 6.44], [24, 6.44, 6.66], [25, 6.66, 6.84], [26, 6.84, 7.1]]}, {"text": "Since it is static, there is not backend database other than static hosting .json files, which could be a thing…", "block": 17, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b2a43105a36ed47ae556abdb041730901745f3460cd0f296aced37053d163958.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.42], [2, 0.42, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.96], [4, 1.36, 1.44], [5, 1.44, 1.6], [6, 1.6, 1.78], [9, 2.66, 2.98], [10, 2.98, 3.22], [11, 3.22, 3.56], [13, 3.94, 4.5], [14, 4.5, 4.86], [15, 5.16, 5.36], [16, 5.36, 5.5], [17, 5.5, 5.64], [18, 5.64, 5.74], [19, 5.74, 6.0]]}, {"text": "Amazon Web Services (free-ish)", "block": 18, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/984d8f871fbde8c84664f69586b78521af5625c5c149ff024b62753cd03dadae.mp3"}, {"text": "For one year, you can utilize the basics of AWS for free.", "block": 19, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d83a28fe1d66f25f85a78e60c22a6509f2b90c79efa0f9219ea32344f834678e.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.74], [3, 0.74, 1.2], [4, 1.2, 1.34], [5, 1.34, 1.66], [6, 1.66, 1.9], [7, 1.9, 2.2], [8, 2.2, 2.42], [9, 2.42, 2.78], [10, 2.78, 3.22], [11, 3.22, 3.5]]}, {"text": "One big catch here is setting up AWS servers and configuring them can be a weekend project on its own, unless you are familiar with devops.", "block": 19, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/2fb1ddba69002b51c57636c812e01b5be98b5ba3c77fb8e8fbfb1bfdeaedfc09.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.62], [3, 0.62, 0.9], [4, 0.9, 1.12], [5, 1.12, 1.38], [6, 1.38, 1.54], [8, 1.88, 2.44], [9, 2.44, 2.7], [10, 2.7, 3.24], [11, 3.24, 3.4], [12, 3.4, 3.56], [13, 3.56, 3.68], [14, 3.68, 3.78], [16, 4.02, 4.44], [17, 4.44, 4.68], [18, 4.68, 4.84], [19, 4.84, 5.1], [20, 5.1, 5.58], [21, 5.58, 5.78], [22, 5.78, 5.88], [23, 5.88, 6.24], [24, 6.24, 6.64], [25, 6.64, 6.88]]}, {"text": "It is not where near as simple as Heroku and you are limited by the resources of one ec2 machine.", "block": 19, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d8485b9e25c315257ebf181d2caf1552734cc3b8ee61ed180161c9289f470bd5.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.7], [4, 0.7, 0.88], [5, 0.88, 1.1], [6, 1.1, 1.36], [7, 1.36, 1.62], [9, 2.62, 2.78], [10, 2.78, 2.9], [11, 2.9, 3.0], [12, 3.0, 3.36], [13, 3.36, 3.6], [14, 3.6, 3.72], [15, 3.72, 4.22], [16, 4.22, 4.54], [17, 4.54, 4.74], [19, 4.98, 5.38]]}, {"text": "It doesn’t scale well if you plan on hosting a bunch of different projects.", "block": 19, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/faefe6c8164b6a07d0d43f245d6933347b545c1f0c6a40809afb598682687bd2.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.78], [3, 0.78, 1.06], [4, 1.06, 1.28], [5, 1.28, 1.36], [6, 1.36, 1.54], [7, 1.54, 1.72], [8, 1.72, 2.02], [9, 2.02, 2.2], [10, 2.2, 2.36], [11, 2.36, 2.54], [12, 2.54, 2.78], [13, 2.78, 3.3]]}, {"text": "AWS has RDS which makes it super easy to throw up a database.", "block": 20, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/23ef48fdf7e66e800129e15d82c7c522fea7126c16a46e2cb38cbe4699927283.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.42], [1, 0.42, 0.86], [2, 0.86, 1.28], [3, 1.28, 1.54], [4, 1.54, 1.74], [5, 1.74, 1.96], [6, 1.96, 2.28], [7, 2.28, 2.54], [8, 2.54, 2.76], [9, 2.76, 2.98], [10, 2.98, 3.12], [11, 3.12, 3.18], [12, 3.18, 3.48]]}, {"text": "They support mysql, postgres, and a few others.", "block": 20, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/307959bf1a34f4b75416758e5b2236229266b61788f36c534352dfdffe1dc01b.mp3"}, {"text": "OpenShift (use this one!)", "block": 21, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5feff664addc1ec2c00b467aa7d4efb3a1a7f2d7f8baabd23f15afb8f6cf1800.mp3"}, {"text": "OpenShift seems like the best drop in replacement for Heroku.", "block": 22, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f25cae3e4b4c57d650bb573ec5811d38129b6f0e9def402910c16d5702c9bbf7.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.7], [1, 0.7, 1.02], [2, 1.02, 1.24], [3, 1.24, 1.4], [4, 1.4, 1.7], [5, 1.7, 1.92], [6, 1.92, 2.16], [7, 2.16, 2.64], [8, 2.64, 2.92], [9, 2.92, 3.34]]}, {"text": "They have a free tier with reasonably powerful servers.", "block": 22, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ce25239c2ee9dde28cd951575cc654b375af98eab38e3a2155d53e058668387f.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.7], [4, 0.7, 0.98], [5, 0.98, 1.22], [6, 1.22, 1.6], [7, 1.6, 2.16], [8, 2.16, 2.68]]}, {"text": "Unfortunately the database shares the same limited resources the application server utilizes, so you get a bit less than 1GB of storage space for your application and database to share.", "block": 22, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8c42cd79e0ddafafb9bb2c635364cfab1f70f350ee8b08a36580dc98805f5b1e.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.6], [1, 0.82, 0.94], [2, 0.94, 1.2], [3, 1.2, 1.58], [4, 1.58, 1.82], [5, 1.82, 2.04], [6, 2.04, 2.36], [7, 2.36, 2.92], [8, 2.92, 3.18], [9, 3.18, 3.6], [10, 3.6, 4.02], [11, 4.02, 4.68], [12, 5.04, 5.26], [13, 5.26, 5.38], [14, 5.38, 5.54], [15, 5.54, 5.62], [16, 5.62, 5.74], [17, 5.74, 5.96], [18, 5.96, 6.2], [19, 6.2, 6.68], [20, 6.68, 6.92], [21, 6.92, 7.22], [22, 7.22, 7.54], [23, 7.54, 7.76], [24, 7.76, 7.88], [25, 7.88, 8.46], [26, 8.46, 8.74], [27, 8.74, 9.0], [28, 9.0, 9.36], [29, 9.36, 9.58]]}, {"text": "My strategy here is to keep my Heroku database up and just configure my OpenShift application to connect directly to the Heroku one, so I don’t have to deal with shared resources.", "block": 23, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8bda4d3238df0cb011f52928fc4b3401cfbef2d8580d2469c8ff9f7e9364e695.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.56], [2, 0.56, 0.94], [3, 0.94, 1.2], [4, 1.2, 1.32], [5, 1.32, 1.5], [6, 1.5, 1.74], [7, 1.74, 2.12], [8, 2.12, 2.46], [9, 2.46, 2.86], [10, 2.86, 3.18], [11, 3.18, 3.32], [12, 3.32, 3.76], [13, 3.76, 4.02], [14, 4.02, 4.5], [15, 4.5, 5.04], [16, 5.04, 5.44], [17, 5.44, 5.62], [18, 5.62, 6.06], [19, 6.06, 6.26], [20, 6.26, 6.36], [21, 6.36, 6.76], [23, 7.44, 7.56], [24, 7.56, 7.64], [25, 7.64, 7.86], [26, 7.86, 7.96], [27, 7.96, 8.12], [28, 8.12, 8.26], [29, 8.26, 8.46], [30, 8.46, 8.7], [31, 8.7, 9.24]]}, {"text": "This may make my website a little bit slower, but it should be good enough.", "block": 23, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/234d73283f5b0cc06cef323700eb4943e93bd467cf364907383a0f1ddb250cf7.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.66], [4, 0.66, 1.0], [5, 1.0, 1.24], [6, 1.24, 1.4], [7, 1.4, 1.52], [8, 1.52, 2.0], [9, 2.54, 2.72], [10, 2.72, 2.82], [11, 2.82, 3.08], [12, 3.08, 3.28], [13, 3.28, 3.46], [14, 3.46, 3.74]]}, {"text": "Cloud99", "block": 24, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f5d0603671f8f8413fd324b4a95e61c5b5d24fdd8a649a35357ba1f303a5de1f.mp3"}, {"text": "I have heard bad stories about Cloud99 and they were hacked a few years ago, plus they are not free.", "block": 25, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/488899ea8fbf9334d4342ccef383bce1ba165150c5e7fcf8f30372ae5ce63dfd.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.42], [2, 0.42, 0.56], [3, 0.56, 0.76], [4, 0.76, 1.22], [5, 1.22, 1.5], [7, 2.24, 2.6], [8, 2.6, 2.7], [9, 2.7, 2.82], [10, 2.82, 3.08], [11, 3.08, 3.22], [12, 3.22, 3.36], [13, 3.36, 3.6], [14, 3.6, 3.96], [15, 4.32, 4.58], [16, 4.58, 4.8], [17, 4.8, 4.9], [18, 4.9, 5.06], [19, 5.06, 5.36]]}, {"text": "My advice is to stay away.", "block": 25, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ecf11553c72c6de9cab33cb5edb6e1e6e2c4238ac65b1bd336d089ecc27592dc.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.48], [2, 0.48, 0.84], [3, 0.84, 0.98], [4, 0.98, 1.22], [5, 1.22, 1.48]]}, {"text": "Free email", "block": 26, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/759948fc03e116bcb24dbe0f8f38910134927fac912cb1fb98010a207f557c18.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.6]]}, {"text": "Having an @gmail.com account as the linked support email for your side project is so not classy.", "block": 27, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/0f78cba8ab9e6869adbd4abed9e7ea659fba9193f903e0ea37f4de6c145a0f28.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [1, 0.3, 0.6], [3, 1.42, 1.9], [4, 1.9, 2.12], [5, 2.12, 2.26], [6, 2.26, 2.48], [7, 2.48, 2.9], [8, 2.9, 3.26], [9, 3.26, 3.46], [10, 3.46, 3.6], [11, 3.6, 3.84], [12, 3.84, 4.32], [13, 4.32, 4.58], [14, 4.58, 4.8], [15, 4.8, 5.0], [16, 5.0, 5.4]]}, {"text": "You can configure your free custom domain with Zoho and be able to email your customers from a more legit looking domain.", "block": 27, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/bb881b1e05cd51bbbc49bb81438b72bac43d0c39a242bcb281910fba9e1fcbed.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.74], [3, 0.74, 0.94], [4, 0.94, 1.16], [5, 1.16, 1.54], [6, 1.54, 1.94], [7, 1.94, 2.22], [9, 2.62, 2.9], [10, 2.9, 3.06], [11, 3.06, 3.18], [12, 3.18, 3.34], [13, 3.34, 3.56], [14, 3.56, 3.78], [15, 3.78, 4.24], [16, 4.24, 4.56], [17, 4.56, 4.68], [18, 4.68, 4.92], [19, 4.92, 5.3], [20, 5.3, 5.62], [21, 5.62, 5.98]]}, {"text": "Be sure to configure your MX records properly so your new domain doesn’t get sent to the spam folder.", "block": 27, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9fae5b7bb50562c9beba49ed28e18c6901010086ccad785a7e0709ef5b4373ae.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.5], [3, 0.5, 0.94], [4, 0.94, 1.24], [5, 1.24, 1.46], [7, 1.92, 2.48], [8, 2.48, 2.94], [9, 2.94, 3.14], [10, 3.14, 3.34], [11, 3.34, 3.7], [12, 3.7, 4.44], [13, 4.44, 4.56], [14, 4.56, 4.78], [15, 4.78, 5.02], [16, 5.02, 5.1], [17, 5.1, 5.3], [18, 5.3, 5.64]]}, {"text": "Free transactional email sending", "block": 28, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9cf0d29cf99f9acacdb308c4ae13a9ee319516c75b2baed84ce0e3740bd09e94.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 1.06], [2, 1.06, 1.42], [3, 1.42, 1.86]]}, {"text": "I really like Mailchimp’s Mandrill.", "block": 29, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/034734462c78bc53e820e1c6c4baf460385c435792e665b5e04b57978f305309.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.72], [3, 0.72, 1.34]]}, {"text": "I have been using them for years and haven’t had any problems.", "block": 29, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/2cfc354ad8d54fe39dbecc7903f01fed0cf531e266038c545a7a8946ccb00e69.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [2, 0.26, 0.34], [3, 0.34, 0.56], [4, 0.56, 0.76], [5, 0.76, 0.92], [6, 0.92, 1.24], [7, 1.24, 1.46], [8, 1.46, 1.72], [9, 1.72, 1.88], [10, 1.88, 2.06], [11, 2.06, 2.46]]}, {"text": "They offer a generous number of emails sent (10k) to be exact and don’t limit their services in features, just mailing volume.", "block": 29, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/4a78469432950a6e510a084c64c1b4d9a01a7ac2e706e380416c06426786c894.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.56], [2, 0.56, 0.74], [3, 0.74, 1.04], [4, 1.04, 1.38], [5, 1.38, 1.56], [6, 1.56, 1.82], [7, 1.82, 2.22], [8, 2.22, 2.96], [9, 2.96, 3.28], [10, 3.28, 3.42], [11, 3.42, 3.78], [12, 3.78, 4.1], [13, 4.1, 4.34], [14, 4.34, 4.52], [15, 4.52, 4.7], [16, 4.7, 5.12], [18, 5.36, 5.68], [19, 6.14, 6.28], [20, 6.28, 6.58], [21, 6.58, 7.0]]}, {"text": "Free SSL certs", "block": 30, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b53bd7e93be63462efefbf8f642dec37cc4b8b1f24ad8c8467c8602834c5fc45.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 1.0], [2, 1.0, 1.8]]}, {"text": "Another sweet trick you can do for your side project websites is to use Cloudflare to deliver valid SSL certificates for your projects.", "block": 31, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/18d8ae6147fdd8c049e5e0929282af64257713395f199cf221275b708c6aded9.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.36, 0.72], [2, 0.72, 0.98], [3, 0.98, 1.18], [4, 1.18, 1.32], [5, 1.32, 1.48], [6, 1.48, 1.66], [7, 1.66, 1.8], [8, 1.8, 2.04], [9, 2.04, 2.46], [10, 2.46, 2.94], [11, 2.94, 3.26], [12, 3.26, 3.44], [13, 3.44, 3.66], [15, 4.24, 4.54], [16, 4.54, 4.9], [17, 4.9, 5.48], [18, 5.48, 6.18], [19, 6.18, 6.68], [20, 6.68, 7.0], [21, 7.0, 7.12], [22, 7.12, 7.58]]}, {"text": "From an SEO perspective, google loves SSL and from a safety and privacy perspective users love SSL.", "block": 31, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b0d087e9192fdbfcb95d9924b4a1d9eb9cb243b85cba57b2ac168d1071d660c1.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.7], [3, 0.7, 1.32], [4, 1.88, 2.06], [5, 2.06, 2.4], [6, 2.4, 2.9], [7, 3.1, 3.16], [8, 3.16, 3.32], [9, 3.32, 3.44], [10, 3.44, 3.78], [11, 3.78, 3.92], [12, 3.92, 4.26], [13, 4.26, 5.06], [14, 5.32, 5.5], [15, 5.5, 5.8], [16, 5.8, 6.36]]}, {"text": "You can read up on how to do with here.", "block": 31, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/af25cdde37d28075aae87ffb330ab60b6de3918e04a150629f8c120b83723ec9.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.74], [4, 0.74, 0.96], [5, 0.96, 1.14], [6, 1.14, 1.26], [7, 1.26, 1.48], [8, 1.48, 1.86], [9, 1.86, 2.28]]}, {"text": "It took me 15 minutes to configure https://kcoleman.me and AtlantaStartupJobs.com to be behind Cloudflare.", "block": 32, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/558d9930e679e07851cad081165ddac2f27398aa85fbf1d26542649b75a1509c.mp3"}]}